  "op": "lint",
  "sprint": {
    "brief": "planning v1.0.0 — EDD PLANNING — a frozen upstream artifact becomes an enforced, buildable plan: FRAME → CARVE → SEQUENCE → DISPATCH.",
    "gen": 0,
    "retry_budget": 3,
    "macros": [
      {
        "id": "frame",
        "title": "FRAME",
        "instructions": "## Macro FRAME — EDD planning protocol\n\nLoad `docs/edd/planning-protocol.md@sha256:41808c99e71d` (the FRAME rows and the\nDefinitions it depends on) and `docs/edd/doctrine.md` (the evidence ladder, the\nstakes procedure, the independence rules). Their MUST clauses bind; do NOT restate\nthem here — this prompt only routes.\n\nThe frozen upstream artifact (or, standalone, the raw task) arrives as\n`initial_context`. Read it in full before writing anything.\n\nSub-states run in order: intake → bearings → terms → framed (gate). For the current\nsub-state, load and follow its dispatch prompt and invoke its skill:\n  - intake:   docs/edd/prompts/planning/01-intake.md    · skill plan-frame\n  - bearings: docs/edd/prompts/planning/02-bearings.md  · skill plan-bearings\n  - terms:    docs/edd/prompts/planning/03-terms.md     · skill plan-terms\nEach emits its owned fields of `plan/frame.json` against\n`docs/edd/templates/planning/frame.tmpl.json`.\n\nThe `framed` gate is mechanical: run `docs/edd/tools/plan-check --phase frame` and\nsubmit each criterion below as evidence only when its PASS line is present. A gate is\nnot a formality — a criterion you cannot make pass is a FRAME defect, not a checkbox\nto assert."
      },
      {
        "id": "carve",
        "title": "CARVE",
        "instructions": "## Macro CARVE — EDD planning protocol\n\nLoad `docs/edd/planning-protocol.md@sha256:41808c99e71d` (the CARVE rows, the\nScope-tiers and Hotspot definitions). MUST clauses bind; do not restate.\n\nConsume `plan/frame.json` (frozen by FRAME). Sub-states run in order:\ncarve → size → carved (gate). For the current sub-state, load its dispatch prompt and\nskill:\n  - carve: docs/edd/prompts/planning/05-carve.md · skill plan-carve\n  - size:  docs/edd/prompts/planning/06-size.md  · skill plan-size\nThey emit `plan/packages.json` against `docs/edd/templates/planning/packages.tmpl.json`.\nconflict_pairs and hotspots are COMPUTED at the carve transition (run\n`docs/edd/tools/plan-graph --conflict`), never asserted.\n\nThe `carved` gate is mechanical: `docs/edd/tools/plan-check --phase carve`."
      },
      {
        "id": "sequence",
        "title": "SEQUENCE",
        "instructions": "## Macro SEQUENCE — EDD planning protocol\n\nLoad `docs/edd/planning-protocol.md@sha256:41808c99e71d` (the SEQUENCE rows, the\nenablement table, the Constants table). MUST clauses bind; do not restate. This macro\nruns only when there is more than one package; a single-package plan renders the short\nform and its sub-states collapse to the wait register.\n\nConsume `plan/packages.json`. Sub-states run in order: waits → order → forecast →\nsequenced (gate). Load each sub-state's dispatch prompt and skill:\n  - waits:    docs/edd/prompts/planning/08-waits.md    · skill plan-waits\n  - order:    docs/edd/prompts/planning/09-order.md    · skill plan-order\n  - forecast: docs/edd/prompts/planning/10-forecast.md · skill plan-forecast\nThey emit `plan/sequence.json` against `docs/edd/templates/planning/sequence.tmpl.json`\n(order via `docs/edd/tools/plan-graph --order`).\n\nThe `sequenced` gate is mechanical: `docs/edd/tools/plan-check --phase sequence`."
      },
      {
        "id": "dispatch",
        "title": "DISPATCH",
        "instructions": "## Macro DISPATCH — EDD planning protocol\n\nLoad `docs/edd/planning-protocol.md@sha256:41808c99e71d` (the DISPATCH rows) and\n`docs/edd/doctrine.md` (holdout, independence). MUST clauses bind; do not restate.\n\nConsume `plan/frame.json`, `plan/packages.json`, `plan/sequence.json`. Sub-states run\nin order: policy → packets → hostile_read → tripwires → frozen (gate). Load each\nsub-state's dispatch prompt and skill:\n  - policy:       docs/edd/prompts/planning/12-policy.md        · skill plan-policy\n  - packets:      docs/edd/prompts/planning/13-packets.md       · skill plan-packet\n  - hostile_read: docs/edd/prompts/planning/14-hostile-read.md  · skill plan-hostile-read\n  - tripwires:    docs/edd/prompts/planning/15-tripwires.md     · skill plan-tripwires\nThey emit `plan/manifest.json` (policy, packets, holdout, tripwires) and the\nhostile-read verdict object.\n\nhostile_read runs in a COLD context: a fresh session or a second agent holding only the\nfrozen artifacts, never the context that wrote the plan. If you produced this plan in\nthis context you are disqualified from reviewing it — spawn a fresh one. A FIXES-NEEDED\nverdict loops DISPATCH; it does not pass. Solo, record `reviewer: operator`.\n\nThe `frozen` gate is mechanical: `docs/edd/tools/plan-check --phase dispatch`. It\nfreezes the plan — what BUILD consumes."
      }
    ],
